{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Balaam saw that it was good, etc.</b> He said: I no longer need to inquire of the Holy One, blessed be He, for He does not wish to curse them." "<b>He did not go as time after time.</b> As he had done the two times." "<b>To meet auguries.</b> To divine — perhaps YHWH would chance to meet him at his will. He said: Since He is willing and unwilling to curse them, I will recall their sins, and the curse will take effect upon the recalling of their sins." "<b>And he set his face toward the wilderness.</b> As the Targum renders."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:30.474446508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}